/**
 * Event Modes - event modes and Dynamic Fog for zombie escape, all in one admin menu.
 * The code lives in em_modules/: common.sp (access check, shared tags), modes.sp (VIP, Heal Beacon,
 * round tracking, main menu), fog.sp, weapons.sp, gungame.sp, potato.sp, buddy.sp, lightning.sp, quiz.sp,
 * rlgl.sp, simon.sp, teleport.sp, invert.sp, blackout.sp, ghost.sp, boss.sp, quake.sp, hero.sp, laststand.sp,
 * lava.sp, drop.sp, trivia.sp, hotseat.sp, the 20 hazards (meteor.sp ... frenzy.sp), doublejump.sp,
 * physics.sp (shared speed and gravity), roulette.sp, integrations.sp (optional Zombie Reloaded, EntWatch,
 * DynamicChannels) and settings.sp (generated by em_modules/gen_settings.py - rerun it after adding a
 * setting to a mode's menu: python em_modules/gen_settings.py .).
 * Config files in configs/eventmodes/: dynamicfog.cfg, trivia.cfg, hotseat.cfg; the plugin writes
 * settings.cfg (all menu settings) and gungame.cfg (damage per gun) itself.
 *
 * Access: anyone who has access to "sm_eventload" (CheckCommandAccess).
 *         Change who that is with an override in configs/admin_overrides.cfg, e.g.  "sm_eventload" "z"
 *
 * Commands
 *   sm_em / sm_eventmode  (!em)    admin menu: Event Roulette, 7 categories of modes, Admin tools
 *   sm_em <mode> [on|off]          switch a mode from chat, console or rcon (sm_em list for the names);
 *                                  also sm_em roulette [on|off], sm_em stop, sm_em save, sm_em load
 *   sm_fog                (!fog)   fog in chat: on/off, distances, colours, presets (fine-tuning)
 *   sm_emvip              (!emvip) anyone: who the VIPs / heal beacon carriers are right now
 *   sm_emgun              (!emgun) anyone: get your Gun Game gun / Random Weapons set back (15 s cooldown)
 *
 * VIP mode
 *   When the first zombie appears each round, a random human becomes the VIP (or an admin picks one).
 *   Everyone sees the VIP's name on screen. If the VIP dies or gets infected, every human is slain
 *   (or, if set in the menu, a new VIP is picked). If the VIP turns into a mother zombie, a new VIP is
 *   picked instead - that isn't the humans' fault.
 *
 * Heal Beacon mode
 *   A human carries a beacon ring. Humans inside the radius heal, humans outside lose health every
 *   second. If the beacon carrier dies or is infected, a new one is picked (or all humans are slain).
 *
 * Random Weapons
 *   Every human gets a random weapon set (each their own, or everyone the same). Once given, only kevlar
 *   and HE grenades can be bought and other guns can't be picked up (map items still can).
 *
 * Gun Game
 *   Everyone starts on a pistol; damage to zombies levels your gun up a 24-gun ladder. After the last
 *   gun you prestige: back to the pistol plus an HE grenade. Same buy lock as Random Weapons.
 *
 * Hot Potato
 *   A human holds a potato with a countdown and passes it by knifing a human or pressing E next to one.
 *   Whoever holds it at zero explodes, hurting humans close by.
 *
 * Buddy System
 *   Humans are paired up when the zombies come. If your buddy falls, you die (or bleed). Optionally
 *   you bleed while too far from your buddy.
 *
 * Lightning Strikes
 *   Every few seconds bolts land near random humans after a red warning ring, hurting anyone inside.
 *
 * Math Quiz
 *   Every so often players get a simple sum (each their own, or all the same) and type the answer in
 *   chat: one try, a reward for right answers, an optional penalty for wrong or missing ones.
 *
 * Red Light, Green Light
 *   The screen flips between GREEN and RED. Holding a movement key on red costs health.
 *
 * Simon Says
 *   "SIMON SAYS: CROUCH!" - do it in time; a trick "JUMP!" without Simon - don't. Wrong costs health.
 *
 * Event Roulette
 *   A second into each round it turns on random modes from a pool the admins choose, and turns them
 *   off at round end. Modes switched on by hand are left alone.
 *
 * Fog
 *   Nothing is touched until an admin changes the fog. Then every env_fog_controller on the map (plus one
 *   of our own for maps without fog) and the 3D skybox fog show the admin's values, re-applied so map
 *   logic can't undo them. Presets: configs/eventmodes/dynamicfog.cfg. "Back to the map's own fog" / !fog reset
 *   restores the map's values.
 *
 * Everything stays on round after round until turned off, and switches off on map change.
 */

#include <sourcemod>
#include <sdktools>
#include <cstrike>
#include <sdkhooks>

#pragma semicolon 1
#pragma newdecls required

#define PLUGIN_VERSION "2.0.0"

#include "em_modules/common.sp"
